Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 01:03:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] Keep the datatype and language tag of constant literals

A constant object map whose constant is a typed or language-tagged literal
(rml:object true, rml:object "train"@en) gave a simple literal: the
datatype and the language tag were lost. RML-Core gives the literal as it
is (RMLTC0028a and 0028c, kg-construct/rml-core).

The normalizer now turns the datatype (other than xsd:string) or the
language tag of such a constant into a constant datatype map or language
map, unless the object map has one. Test: test/constant-literal-annotations.
